+# Final correction selection
+
+Owns complete final correction trials, fallback selection, electrical/physical-drive
+verification and final publication. Shared native-seat replay, acceptance, ledger,
+report and resource computations stay in `roomeq-playback`. Production depends on
+lower owners and shared workflow contracts; it has no routed/workflow dependency.
+
+The three canonical end-to-end optimization cases remain in workflow with their
+original ignored states, 600,000-iteration budget, seeds and assertions. Other
+finalization unit cases move with the entire production implementation. The
+existing full-strength diagnostic helper is exposed only by `test-support`,
+enabled through the workflow dev-dependency. It adds no default production API.
+
+This is an experimental full extraction. Compiler, native scope, correctness,
+coverage, paired runtime/build measurements and a measured accept/reject decision
+are required before adoption. No performance claim is implied by this boundary.
